===Etymology===
Composed of [[Ekavian]] Serbo-Croatian {{term|beo|bȅo|white|lang=sh}} (from {{proto|Slavic|bělъ|lang=sh}}) and {{term|grad|grȃd|city|lang=sh}} (from {{proto|Slavic|gordъ|lang=sh}}). The city is named after the white wall of the fortress that enclosed the city. See also {{term|Biograd|lang=sh}}, {{term|Белгород|Бе́лгород|tr=Bélgorod|sc=Cyrl|lang=ru}}, {{term|Białogard}}.

